window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-sakura-airi"]=[{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v1-p110-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi campus store debut  the broken camera campus convenience electronics store  late april  a quiet  bespectacled girl standing alone by the digital camera display rack  wears glasses with large frames  long hair draped forward to obscure her facial features  wearing the anhs uniform  holds a compact digital camera with a damaged broken casing in both hands  staring at the replacement models with intense anxiety  when ayanokoji steps into the aisle nearby  she flinches in alarm  avoids eye contact completely  clutches her broken camera tightly to her chest  and hurriedly flees down the aisle  pathologically shy  hyper sensitive to the presence of others  deeply attached to digital photography","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v1-p110-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Campus store debut: the broken camera<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.110–111<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Campus convenience/electronics store, late April.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">A quiet, bespectacled girl standing alone by the digital camera display rack. Wears glasses with large frames, long hair draped forward to obscure her facial features, wearing the ANHS uniform.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q action\">Holds a compact digital camera with a damaged/broken casing in both hands, staring at the replacement models with intense anxiety.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Ayanokōji steps into the aisle nearby, she flinches in alarm, avoids eye contact completely, clutches her broken camera tightly to her chest, and hurriedly flees down the aisle.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pathologically shy, hyper-sensitive to the presence of others, deeply attached to digital photography.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p10-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 1  sakura airi s soliloquy  the volume opens in her pov whole first person monologue chapter   the only non ayanokoji pov chapter opening in year 1  vol  2  foreshadows her role as  an unexpected witness   ch 4   i don t know how to interact with other people  i m bad at talking while making eye contact  i m horrible with crowds  i don t remember how or when i became so hopeless   however  one thing i do know for certain is that a person cannot live entirely in isolation  no matter how much i may love my solitude  i can t remain totally by myself  so  i came up with a solution  i would adopt a false face and hide my true self  then  i wouldn t be completely honest  but i could be a version of myself  i could continue to live in this dark  lonely world  self aware about her condition  frames the false face as a deliberate  solution  not an accident   same masking logic she later applies to photography   is everyone else putting on a facade  just like me  or do most people show their true selves to the outside world  since i can t connect with people  i suppose there s no way for me to find out the answer  therefore  i remain alone   i m all right by myself  i m all right with being alone   i  i want to connect with someone from the bottom of my heart  her interior voice  short declarative confessions  self questioning  closing cadence  and so i will continue to live quietly  with my eyes downcast  alone  paradox locked in at volume start  wants a heart to heart connection while believing connection is impossible for her   the engine of her year 1  vol  2 arc","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1 &quot;Sakura Airi&#x27;s Soliloquy&quot;: the volume opens in her POV<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.10<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;I don&#x27;t know how to interact with other people. I&#x27;m bad at talking while making eye contact. I&#x27;m horrible with crowds. I don&#x27;t remember how or when I became so hopeless.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;However, one thing I do know for certain is that a person cannot live entirely in isolation. No matter how much I may love my solitude, I can&#x27;t remain totally by myself. So, I came up with a solution. I would adopt a false face…<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;Is everyone else putting on a façade, just like me? Or do most people show their true selves to the outside world? Since I can&#x27;t connect with people, I suppose there&#x27;s no way for me to find out the answer. Therefore, I remain…<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Whole first-person monologue chapter — the only non-Ayanokōji POV chapter opening in Year 1, Vol. 2; foreshadows her role as &quot;An Unexpected Witness&quot; (Ch.4).<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;However, one thing I do know for certain is that a person cannot live entirely in isolation. No matter how much I may love my solitude, I can&#x27;t remain totally by myself. So, I came up with a solution. I would adopt a false face and hide my true self. Then, I wouldn&#x27;t be completely honest, but I could be a version of myself. I could continue to live in this dark, lonely world.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Self-aware about her condition; frames the false face as a deliberate &quot;solution,&quot; not an accident — same masking logic she later applies to photography.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Is everyone else putting on a façade, just like me? Or do most people show their true selves to the outside world? Since I can&#x27;t connect with people, I suppose there&#x27;s no way for me to find out the answer. Therefore, I remain alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m all right by myself. I&#x27;m all right with being alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I… I want to connect with someone from the bottom of my heart.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Her interior voice: short declarative confessions, self-questioning, closing cadence &quot;And so I will continue to live quietly, with my eyes downcast. Alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Paradox locked in at volume start: wants a heart-to-heart connection while believing connection is impossible for her — the engine of her Year 1, Vol. 2 arc.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p12-1\">→ After: Ch.2 opening: she stumbles on Sudou&#x27;s three-on-one brawl (the witness birthed)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p12-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner","w":"sudou-ken sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 2 opening  she stumbles on sudou s three on one brawl  the witness birthed  evening of june 30  inside a school building with a staircase  the  special building  named sudou s account p 30 31  while hunting for a good selfie spot  sakura finds three male students writhing on the floor and a red haired boy standing over them   the timing couldn t have been worse  while searching for a place to take a good selfie  i stumbled into something  even a certain famous  diminutive detective would have held his breath when witnessing such a tense situation   his right fist was covered in blood from the students he d pummeled  this was the first brawl i d ever witnessed  terror overrides etiquette but not habit   though i was terrified  i began capturing the scene with my camera  the shutter didn t make a sound  panic freeze   after taking the pictures  i asked myself what i was doing  i couldn t think clearly in my panicked state  my legs didn t obey my command to move  like i was paralyzed   i d heard that that when someone was involved in a crisis  his or her body would lock up  exactly like what was happening now   sic   doubled  that  in corpus   i d hate it if someone were to spot me and involve me in this mess  if that happened  it would cast a dark cloud over my otherwise peaceful school life  sudou  sensing movement  calls  is someone there  toward her hiding spot  she escapes by seconds   i d successfully escaped by a hair s breadth  if i d lagged a mere two seconds  he probably would ve seen me  document first  confront never instinct  she photographs the fight but flees rather than intervene or report  self protection through invisibility  unseen witness to his brawl  nearly discovered by him   she does not know his name to face link yet beyond  sudou kun  heard in his taunts   2 2 lunch  observed by ayanokoji  still eating alone  hunched over a homemade bento  the glasses and plain girl reputation  at one time ike had made a ruckus about how large her breasts were  but because she was considered plain  everyone quickly lost interest","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 opening: she stumbles on Sudou&#x27;s three-on-one brawl (the witness birthed)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.12–13<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Evening of June 30, inside a school building with a staircase (the &quot;special building,&quot; named Sudou&#x27;s account p.30–31). While hunting for a good selfie spot, Sakura finds three male students writhing on the floor and a red-haired boy standing over them. Sudou, sensing movement, calls &quot;Is someone there?&quot; toward her hiding spot; she escapes by seconds: &quot;I’d successfully escaped by a hair’s breadth. If I’d lagged a mere two seconds, he probably would’ve seen me.&quot; §2.2 lunch, observed by Ayanokōji: still eating alone, hunched over a homemade bento; the glasses-and-plain-girl reputation (&quot;At one time Ike had made a ruckus about how large her breasts were, but because she was considered plain, everyone quickly lost interest.&quot;).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;The timing couldn’t have been worse. While searching for a place to take a good selfie, I stumbled into something. Even a certain famous, diminutive detective would have held his breath when witnessing such a tense situation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;His right fist was covered in blood from the students he’d pummeled. This was the first brawl I’d ever witnessed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">Panic freeze: &quot;After taking the pictures, I asked myself what I was doing. I couldn’t think clearly in my panicked state... My legs didn’t obey my command to move, like I was paralyzed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Terror overrides etiquette but not habit: &quot;Though I was terrified, I began capturing the scene with my camera. The shutter didn’t make a sound.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I’d heard that that when someone was involved in a crisis, his or her body would lock up, exactly like what was happening now.&quot; (sic — doubled &quot;that&quot; in corpus)<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I’d hate it if someone were to spot me and involve me in this mess. If that happened, it would cast a dark cloud over my otherwise peaceful school life.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Document-first, confront-never instinct: she photographs the fight but flees rather than intervene or report; self-protection through invisibility.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Unseen witness to his brawl; nearly discovered by him — she does not know his name-to-face link yet beyond &quot;Sudou-kun&quot; heard in his taunts.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p10-1\">← Before: Ch.1 &quot;Sakura Airi&#x27;s Soliloquy&quot;: the volume opens in her POV<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the witness sits in the room and says nothing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p40-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 3  the witness sits in the room and says nothing chabashira puts the ask to the classroom   if anyone here witnessed the fight  please raise your hand     no students raised their hands in response to her question  this is inference  stated as inference  sakura was in that homeroom  pp 40 43 is class d s classroom  and she is a class d student  but chapter 3 never singles her out  never names her  and never says whether she looked up  all this page can assert is that no hand went up  kushida re asks the same question in a form a witness could answer privately    if anyone knows someone who saw what happened  whether it s someone in class  a friend  or an upperclassman  please tell me  you can contact me at any time    the one line in the chapter that would have been safe for her to answer  and she does not  she holds the only neutral visual record of pp 12 13   silent camera photographs she has not shown anyone   and chapter 3 closes with it still hidden  the window that her silence consumes is fixed and public   we ll make our final judgment next tuesday  taking into account any eyewitnesses and evidence  and  in order to check for witnesses  every teacher will inform their classes of the details of this incident  the school is now actively canvassing every class in the year for her  ak  in a classroom with  about one third of our class remained in the room   suddenly  i felt a sensation  like someone was watching me  i turned around  the text never says who watched him and never resolves it inside the chapter  do not read it as sakura   it is an unanswered beat  not a link  her chapter 1 creed  and so i will continue to live quietly  with my eyes downcast  alone  is what the whole chapter quietly costs sudou  invisibility works  and it works on the class s behalf too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the witness sits in the room and says nothing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.40–65<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira puts the ask to the classroom: &quot;If anyone here witnessed the fight, please raise your hand.&quot; — &quot;No students raised their hands in response to her question.&quot; Kushida re-asks the same question in a form a witness could answer privately — &quot;If anyone knows someone who saw what happened, whether it’s someone in class, a friend, or an upperclassman, please tell me. You can contact me at any time.&quot; — the one line in the chapter that would have been safe for her to answer, and she does not.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> This is inference, stated as inference: Sakura was in that homeroom (pp.40–43 is Class D&#x27;s classroom, and she is a Class D student), but Chapter 3 never singles her out, never names her, and never says whether she looked up. All this page can assert is that no hand went up.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> She holds the only neutral visual record of pp.12–13 — silent-camera photographs she has not shown anyone — and Chapter 3 closes with it still hidden.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The window that her silence consumes is fixed and public: &quot;We’ll make our final judgment next Tuesday, taking into account any eyewitnesses and evidence,&quot; and &quot;In order to check for witnesses, every teacher will inform their classes of the details of this incident.&quot; The school is now actively canvassing every class in the year for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> AK, in a classroom with &quot;about one third of our class remained in the room&quot;: &quot;Suddenly, I felt a sensation, like someone was watching me. I turned around.&quot; The text never says who watched him and never resolves it inside the chapter. Do not read it as Sakura — it is an unanswered beat, not a link.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her Chapter 1 creed (&quot;And so I will continue to live quietly, with my eyes downcast. Alone.&quot;) is what the whole chapter quietly costs Sudou: invisibility works, and it works on the class&#x27;s behalf too.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.2 opening: she stumbles on Sudou&#x27;s three-on-one brawl (the witness birthed)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p77-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: she is named, and stays a rumour to the people who sit near her<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p77-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4  4 1  she is named  and stays a rumour to the people who sit near her  sakura san    the first time anyone in class d says her name out loud in the volume  spoken by horikita in ayanokoji s room  horikita s proof  which is entirely about sakura s own behaviour   when kushida san said that she was looking for a witness in class  sakura looked down  a lot of students were staring at kushida san  sakura was the only one who didn t appear interested  she is now identified as the witness by the one student who was watching the wrong student  and horikita s confidence is absolute   no  sakura san is undoubtedly the witness  her actions confirmed it  although she may not admit to it  she is definitely the one  nobody in the room can place her body in the room  sudou and yamauchi  exchanged looks  they didn t seem to know who sakura even was  the seating is argued wrong twice before kushida fixes it    she sits diagonally ahead of sudou kun to the right  sudou s admission of the class s real opinion of her   diagonally ahead to the right  i can t remember at all  i m sure there s someone there  though  ak s verdict on why that matters for the case   sakura certainly didn t stand out very much  the fact we didn t really know her was a problem  ike  asked to describe her  offers one fact   would it help if i said she has the biggest boobs in class  her boobs are insanely huge    and yamauchi converts it into a stereotype on the spot   oh  she s that plain girl with glasses  right  kushida defends her  in the only defence she gets in the chapter   it s not good to remember people based on something like that  ikekun  that s pathetic  her phone goes unanswered when kushida calls   she listened to her phone ring for about 20 seconds  but then she shook her head and hung up    ak s reading   sakura might just be pretending to be out  too  kushida s account of what sakura actually gave her   she gave me her contact information  but she doesn t know me very well  she might be confused if i tried to call her  her invisibility is total enough to make the room s memory unreliable  sudou misnames her on the spot    this sakura  or kokura  or whoever    and yamauchi disowns having ever confessed to her  it wasn t sakura  it was a girl from the next class over  not a gloomy and ugly girl like sakura  then drops the subject mid sentence by claiming a message  even the class s most charitable description is an apology for her   it s certainly true that sakura was plain  but she wasn t ugly  i d never gotten a good look at her face before  but she seemed to have very nice features  even so  i couldn t say that with complete confidence  probably because sakura had so little presence  the plan the chapter ends on is to let one girl approach her alone   well  i ll try to talk to her myself tomorrow  i think she might be on her guard if a lot of people approach her  kushida said   and ak s gloss   if kushida couldn t manage it  then i doubted anyone else would be able to get through to sakura  the only class d student who ever looked at her closely is the one who does not like being looked at  horikita s read of sakura s downcast eyes is the chapter s hinge and sakura never learns it happened  kushida holds her contact number  her seating position and the class s only defence of her  and still cannot reach her by phone  all of this is class d talking about her in a room she is not in  chapter 4 gives her no line of her own until her own section later in the chapter  nothing here is her choice","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p77-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.1: she is named, and stays a rumour to the people who sit near her<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.77–82<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Nobody in the room can place her body in the room: Sudou and Yamauchi &quot;exchanged looks. They didn’t seem to know who Sakura even was&quot;; the seating is argued wrong twice before Kushida fixes it — &quot;She sits diagonally ahead of Sudou-kun to the right.&quot; Kushida defends her, in the only defence she gets in the chapter: &quot;It’s not good to remember people based on something like that, Ikekun! That’s pathetic.&quot; The plan the chapter ends on is to let one girl approach her alone: &quot;Well, I’ll try to talk to her myself tomorrow. I think she might be on her guard if a lot of people approach her,&quot; Kushida said — and AK&#x27;s gloss: &quot;If Kushida couldn’t manage it, then I doubted anyone else would be able to get through to Sakura.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sakura-san.&quot; — the first time anyone in Class D says her name out loud in the volume, spoken by Horikita in Ayanokōji&#x27;s room.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Horikita&#x27;s proof, which is entirely about Sakura&#x27;s own behaviour: &quot;When Kushida-san said that she was looking for a witness in class, Sakura looked down. A lot of students were staring at Kushida-san. Sakura was the only one who…<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Sudou&#x27;s admission of the class&#x27;s real opinion of her: &quot;Diagonally ahead to the right? I can’t remember at all. I’m sure there’s someone there, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Horikita&#x27;s proof, which is entirely about Sakura&#x27;s own behaviour: &quot;When Kushida-san said that she was looking for a witness in class, Sakura looked down. A lot of students were staring at Kushida-san. Sakura was the only one who didn’t appear interested.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> She is now identified as the witness by the one student who was watching the wrong student, and Horikita&#x27;s confidence is absolute: &quot;No, Sakura-san is undoubtedly the witness. Her actions confirmed it. Although she may not admit to it, she is definitely the one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77–78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s verdict on why that matters for the case: &quot;Sakura certainly didn’t stand out very much. The fact we didn’t really know her was a problem.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Ike, asked to describe her, offers one fact: &quot;Would it help if I said she has the biggest boobs in class? Her boobs are insanely huge.&quot; — and Yamauchi converts it into a stereotype on the spot: &quot;Oh, she’s that plain girl with glasses, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Her phone goes unanswered when Kushida calls: &quot;She listened to her phone ring for about 20 seconds, but then she shook her head and hung up.&quot; — AK&#x27;s reading: &quot;Sakura might just be pretending to be out, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Kushida&#x27;s account of what Sakura actually gave her: &quot;She gave me her contact information, but she doesn’t know me very well. She might be confused if I tried to call her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her invisibility is total enough to make the room&#x27;s memory unreliable: Sudou misnames her on the spot — &quot;this Sakura, or Kokura, or whoever&quot; — and Yamauchi disowns having ever confessed to her (&quot;It wasn’t Sakura; it was a girl from the next class over. Not a gloomy and ugly girl like Sakura.&quot;), then drops the subject mid-sentence by claiming a message.<span class=\"pg\">p.78, p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Even the class&#x27;s most charitable description is an apology for her: &quot;It’s certainly true that Sakura was plain, but she wasn’t ugly. I’d never gotten a good look at her face before, but she seemed to have very nice features. Even so, I couldn’t say that with complete confidence, probably because Sakura had so little presence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The only Class D student who ever looked at her closely is the one who does not like being looked at; Horikita&#x27;s read of Sakura&#x27;s downcast eyes is the chapter&#x27;s hinge and Sakura never learns it happened.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida holds her contact number, her seating position and the class&#x27;s only defence of her, and still cannot reach her by phone.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> All of this is Class D talking about her in a room she is not in. Chapter 4 gives her no line of her own until her own section later in the chapter; nothing here is her choice.<span class=\"pg\">p.77–82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the witness sits in the room and says nothing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.9–4.10: she lets two people take a camera to a repair counter<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p132-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4  4 9 4 10  she lets two people take a camera to a repair counter she has already arrived and is unnoticed at her own meeting   had sakura really been sitting there the entire time  amazing that we hadn t noticed her at all  not a sign of her presence or aura   i m sorry  i don t stand out much  i suppose  good morning    the first line she speaks aloud in the volume  and she apologises for it before it is needed   oh  you don t need to say that for my sake  ayanokouji kun    his compliment that he felt her presence is declined  her chosen disguise  as read by the boy who has never seen her before   sakura was wearing a hat  and even a surgical face mask  which made it difficult to recognize her at a glance  and  she didn t seem to have a cold  rather  she seemed like the type to wear the mask in order to avoid attention  she must have really hated standing out   yeah  i suppose so  i think i do stand out  especially here    and the mask comes off   sheepishly  she removed her mask   so anyway  about my digital camera  is it okay if we go to the electronics store in the mall    the ask that opens the day  and it is hers   i wonder if they ll fix it right away     sakura  looked rather anxious as she took out her digital camera and held it tight   yeah  it s weird  isn t it    on being asked whether she loves the camera  the repair counter stops her cold in front of two classmates   for some reason  sakura suddenly stopped in her tracks  when i glanced over at her  i noticed she was wearing an expression of blatant fear and revulsion   ah  umm  well  and then  it s nothing     she donned an earnest smile  and walked to the repair counter  kushida takes the entire transaction   sakura  the camera s owner  spoke only when she needed to give her consent or to clarify something  what the camera actually is  technically   when the store clerk opened up the camera to confirm the contents  he saw that part of it had been damaged from the fall  that was why the camera wouldn t turn on properly  fortunately  because sakura still had the warranty card  the item could be repaired free of charge    the contents are never described  the cost of having her address written down by someone else   sakura gently patted her chest and sighed in apparent relief  but when she learned it d take two weeks for the camera to be repaired  she grew discouraged  her shoulders slumped   didn t you feel kind of disgusted    to kushida  about the clerk  the first time she questions someone else s reading of a room   that was kind of what i was trying to get at before  i was scared to go to the repair shop alone because of that  she turns to the quietest of the three for a verdict on a man who frightened her   turning to me  she asked  and then  what do you think  ayanokouji kun   th thank you ayanokouji kun  you really saved me   since you were with me today  kushida san  we completed our task without me having to talk at all  thank you  the camera s history  given unprompted   yeah  i ve liked cameras ever since i was little  my dad bought me one before i entered junior high  and i absolutely fell in love with it  or i suppose you could say that i just love taking pictures  i m not really wellinformed when it comes to this stuff  though    the missing hyphen is the translation s  the one question that makes her physically retreat   sakura stepped backwards  looking quite flustered  then  sakura shut her mouth  and her body stiffened  and  th that s a secret   w well  it s just  it s embarrassing     replied sakura  her cheeks reddening  she looked down as she spoke  whether she photographs people is asked but not answered in this volume  and the asker is not tagged in the translation  only her refusal is hers","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.9–4.10: she lets two people take a camera to a repair counter<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.132–142<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She has already arrived and is unnoticed at her own meeting: &quot;Had Sakura really been sitting there the entire time? Amazing that we hadn’t noticed her at all. Not a sign of her presence or aura.&quot; What the camera actually is, technically: &quot;when the store clerk opened up the camera to confirm the contents, he saw that part of it had been damaged from the fall. That was why the camera wouldn’t turn on properly. Fortunately, because Sakura still had the warranty card, the item could be repaired free of charge.&quot; — the contents are never described. She turns to the quietest of the three for a verdict on a man who frightened her: &quot;Turning to me, she asked&quot; and then &quot;What do you think, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m sorry, I don’t stand out much, I suppose… Good morning,&quot; — the first line she speaks aloud in the volume, and she apologises for it before it is needed.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Oh, you don’t need to say that for my sake, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — his compliment that he felt her presence is declined.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah, I suppose so. I think I do stand out, especially here,&quot; — and the mask comes off: &quot;Sheepishly, she removed her mask.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her chosen disguise, as read by the boy who has never seen her before: &quot;Sakura was wearing a hat, and even a surgical face mask, which made it difficult to recognize her at a glance.&quot; and &quot;She didn’t seem to have a cold. Rather, she seemed like the type to wear the mask in order to avoid attention. She must have really hated standing out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So anyway, about my digital camera. Is it okay if we go to the electronics store in the mall?&quot; — the ask that opens the day, and it is hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I wonder if they’ll fix it right away…&quot; — &quot;Sakura, looked rather anxious as she took out her digital camera and held it tight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah. It’s weird, isn’t it?&quot; — on being asked whether she loves the camera.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The repair counter stops her cold in front of two classmates: &quot;For some reason, Sakura suddenly stopped in her tracks. When I glanced over at her, I noticed she was wearing an expression of blatant fear and revulsion.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ah, umm… Well…&quot; and then &quot;It’s nothing.&quot; — &quot;She donned an earnest smile, and walked to the repair counter.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Kushida takes the entire transaction: &quot;Sakura, the camera’s owner, spoke only when she needed to give her consent or to clarify something.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The cost of having her address written down by someone else: &quot;Sakura gently patted her chest and sighed in apparent relief, but when she learned it’d take two weeks for the camera to be repaired, she grew discouraged. Her shoulders slumped.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Didn’t you feel kind of disgusted?&quot; — to Kushida, about the clerk; the first time she questions someone else&#x27;s reading of a room.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That was kind of what I was trying to get at before… I was scared to go to the repair shop alone because of that…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Th-thank you…Ayanokouji-kun. You really…saved me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Since you were with me today, Kushida-san, we completed our task without me having to talk at all. Thank you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The camera&#x27;s history, given unprompted: &quot;Yeah… I’ve liked cameras ever since I was little. My dad bought me one before I entered junior high, and I absolutely fell in love with it. Or I suppose you could say that I just love taking pictures… I’m not really wellinformed when it comes to this stuff, though.&quot; — the missing hyphen is the translation&#x27;s.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The one question that makes her physically retreat: &quot;Sakura stepped backwards, looking quite flustered.&quot; then &quot;Sakura shut her mouth, and her body stiffened.&quot; and &quot;Th-that’s a secret.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;W-well, it’s just… It’s embarrassing,&quot; — &quot;replied Sakura, her cheeks reddening. She looked down as she spoke.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Whether she photographs people is asked but not answered in this volume, and the asker is not tagged in the translation; only her refusal is hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p77-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: she is named, and stays a rumour to the people who sit near her<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p144-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.10: she is offered a friendship and answers with the case<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p144-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4  4 10  she is offered a friendship and answers with the case kushida asks her to take off her glasses and she refuses in front of a stranger s question   huh  b but that s  my eyesight is so bad  i wouldn t be able to see a thing     sakura put her hand up and waved it  signaling to kushida that she did not want to   umm  thank you for everything today  you really helped me out   i didn t mean to sound that way  i wasn t aware of it  i sound weird    on being told she speaks too formally for a classmate   ah  o okay  i i got it  i ll do my best   i it s okay  i will    and the delivery of even that   sakura kept her eyes down as she spoke  partway through her sentence she began to sputter  and her words faded so much that we couldn t hear them  however  it didn t seem as though she felt uncomfortable  she accepts a change in how she talks rather than lose the two people who came with her   i thought that sakura would have rejected the notion  but she managed to squeak out a few words of agreement   well     sakura spoke in a small voice  but looked straight at us  when our gazes met  however  she immediately averted her eyes   about sudou kun  as my way of saying thanks for today  i  well  that might be a little misleading  but if you like   i i may be able to help you with sudou kun s case    the volume s hinge  offered as a gift in exchange for a day of errands   in her own words  sakura told us that she was the witness   yes  i saw everything  it was a total coincidence  though  i m sure you don t believe me  her stated reason for three weeks of silence   it s okay  i think that if i kept quiet  i d probably come to regret it  i don t want to cause trouble for my classmates  but  if i spoke up as a witness  then i would definitely stand out  i hated the thought of that  i m sorry  she apologises while giving the class exactly what it has been asking for   while sakura apologized to us repeatedly  full of remorse  she also promised kushida that she would testify  everything the case needed was available from her on the first day  what changed is not her courage but her company   she testifies the moment she has two people standing beside her instead of a crowd asking her alone  she tells kushida the camera history  refuses kushida the glasses  and hands kushida the testimony   the friendship is real before the evidence is  he wrote his own name and dorm room on her repair form so she would not have to hand over her address  her first unscheduled call is to him  not to kushida","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.10: she is offered a friendship and answers with the case<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.144–146<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida asks her to take off her glasses and she refuses in front of a stranger&#x27;s question: &quot;Huh?! B-but that’s… My eyesight is so bad, I wouldn’t be able to see a thing…&quot; — &quot;Sakura put her hand up and waved it, signaling to Kushida that she did not want to.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Umm… Thank you for everything today. You really helped me out,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I didn’t mean to sound that way. I wasn’t aware of it… I sound weird?&quot; — on being told she speaks too formally for a classmate.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ah… O-okay… I…I got it. I’ll do my best.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I-It’s okay. I…will.&quot; — and the delivery of even that: &quot;Sakura kept her eyes down as she spoke. Partway through her sentence she began to sputter, and her words faded so much that we couldn’t hear them. However, it didn’t seem as though she felt uncomfortable.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She accepts a change in how she talks rather than lose the two people who came with her: &quot;I thought that Sakura would have rejected the notion, but she managed to squeak out a few words of agreement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well!&quot; — &quot;Sakura spoke in a small voice, but looked straight at us. When our gazes met, however, she immediately averted her eyes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;About Sudou-kun… As my way of saying thanks for today, I… Well, that might be a little misleading, but if you like…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I-I may be able to help you with Sudou-kun’s case.&quot; — the volume&#x27;s hinge, offered as a gift in exchange for a day of errands: &quot;In her own words, Sakura told us that she was the witness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yes. I saw everything. It was a total coincidence, though… I’m sure you don’t believe me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her stated reason for three weeks of silence: &quot;It’s okay… I think that if I kept quiet, I’d probably come to regret it. I…don’t want to cause trouble for my classmates. But, if I spoke up as a witness, then…I would definitely stand out. I hated the thought of that… I’m sorry.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She apologises while giving the class exactly what it has been asking for; &quot;While Sakura apologized to us repeatedly, full of remorse, she also promised Kushida that she would testify.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Everything the case needed was available from her on the first day; what changed is not her courage but her company — she testifies the moment she has two people standing beside her instead of a crowd asking her alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.132–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She tells Kushida the camera history, refuses Kushida the glasses, and hands Kushida the testimony — the friendship is real before the evidence is.<span class=\"pg\">p.142, p.144–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He wrote his own name and dorm room on her repair form so she would not have to hand over her address; her first unscheduled call is to him, not to Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.9–4.10: she lets two people take a camera to a repair counter<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p148-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.11: the call she cannot finish<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p148-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4  4 11  the call she cannot finish the name on ayanokoji s screen that night   i answered sakura s call before it cut out   um  hello  this is sakura   thank you for coming out with me today  the only question she asks anyone in the volume   what were you thinking about    his own report of its shape   sakura asked me a rather ambiguous question   i m sorry  it s nothing  goodnight     sakura ended the call without even giving me a chance to reply  no  please wait  or  hold on  her attempt to reach him fails in silence rather than in words  two stretches of quiet  then an apology  then a hang up   and the volume s last sight of her before class d s punishment falls is a girl who tried to say something twice and did not  she did not call kushida either   a few minutes later  kushida confirmed that she hadn t heard back from sakura  whatever she wanted is not in the record  his reading of it is a guess about the store clerk","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p148-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.11: the call she cannot finish<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.148–150<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The name on Ayanokōji&#x27;s screen that night: &quot;I answered Sakura’s call before it cut out.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Um… Hello. This is Sakura…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Thank you for coming out with me today,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">The only question she asks anyone in the volume: &quot;What were you…thinking about?&quot; — his own report of its shape: &quot;Sakura asked me a rather ambiguous question.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m sorry, it’s nothing. Goodnight.&quot; — &quot;Sakura ended the call without even giving me a chance to reply. No &#x27;please wait&#x27; or &#x27;hold on.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her attempt to reach him fails in silence rather than in words: two stretches of quiet, then an apology, then a hang-up — and the volume&#x27;s last sight of her before Class D&#x27;s punishment falls is a girl who tried to say something twice and did not.<span class=\"pg\">p.149–150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She did not call Kushida either: &quot;A few minutes later, Kushida confirmed that she hadn’t heard back from Sakura.&quot; Whatever she wanted is not in the record; his reading of it is a guess about the store clerk.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p144-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.10: she is offered a friendship and answers with the case<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p163-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: she testifies in the faculty room, and the teacher tests her<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p163-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5  5 2  she testifies in the faculty room  and the teacher tests her after homeroom  the faculty room  kushida brings her forward  ayanokoji waits at the back  out of consideration for sakura   yes  i saw it  she gives the account in full for the first time   none of us  not even the teacher  spoke a single word or even moved until the very end  asked why she is speaking now  she cannot answer cleanly   well  that s  i m just not good at talking with other people   umm  well  it s because our class is in trouble now  and i thought if if i testify  i can help  chabashira s interrogation reduces her physically   sakura hunched and shrank away  much like a frog cornered by a snake  the narrator s reading  kept as his   she should have realized that merely by speaking up  sakura had made great progress   yes    her answer to whether she mustered the courage  the page notes that  sakura  upon imagining this  turned pale and anguished   y yeah    answering kushida   sakura s reply lacked confidence  the deliberation itself is the threat  not the testimony   in addition to having to give her testimony in front of others  she was also going to have to sit alone with sudou   n no  it s fine  she agrees to an arrangement she does not want   she didn t seem to like this at all  but she also didn t have much choice right now","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2: she testifies in the faculty room, and the teacher tests her<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.163–166<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After homeroom, the faculty room. Kushida brings her forward; Ayanokōji waits at the back &quot;out of consideration for Sakura&quot;.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yes. I saw it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Umm… Well, it’s because our…class is in trouble now, and…I thought if…if I testify, I can help…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yes…&quot; — her answer to whether she mustered the courage; the page notes that &quot;Sakura, upon imagining this, turned pale and anguished.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She gives the account in full for the first time: &quot;None of us, not even the teacher, spoke a single word or even moved until the very end.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Asked why she is speaking now, she cannot answer cleanly: &quot;Well… That’s… I’m just not good at talking with other people…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Chabashira&#x27;s interrogation reduces her physically: &quot;Sakura hunched and shrank away, much like a frog cornered by a snake.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator&#x27;s reading, kept as his: &quot;She should have realized that merely by speaking up, Sakura had made great progress.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Y-yeah…&quot; — answering Kushida; &quot;Sakura’s reply lacked confidence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The deliberation itself is the threat, not the testimony: &quot;In addition to having to give her testimony in front of others, she was also going to have to sit alone with Sudou.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;N-no, it’s fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She agrees to an arrangement she does not want: &quot;She didn’t seem to like this at all, but she also didn’t have much choice right now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p148-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.11: the call she cannot finish<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p169-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.4: the night she asks him to come to her room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p169-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5  5 4  the night she asks him to come to her room evening  her dorm room 1106 on the eleventh floor    this was my first time setting foot there    reached by email rather than a call   if i was absent from school tomorrow  what do you think would happen   if it s okay with you  could we meet right now  i m in room 1106   if you could keep this a secret from everyone  that would really help me out   come on in     she greeted me wearing casual clothes   umm  ayanokouji kun  do you remember what you said before  you said i wasn t obligated to step forward  even though i was the witness  you also said it was meaningless to force me to testify   i just don t have any self confidence after all   i ve been terrible at it for so long  i m not good at speaking in front of others  if i m asked to testify in front of the teachers tomorrow  i don t think i ll have the confidence to answer properly  so   ahhhhh  jeez  why am i so completely useless  the outburst is new to him   it was the first time i d seen her like that  and  so she could be animated  i d had no idea  considering her usually depressed look   that s because i m not afraid of your eyes  ayanokouji kun   oh  no  i don t mean the eyes that you ve seen me with  i mean the pupils  way back in the eyes  if you look someone deep in their eyes  you ll understand  i m sorry  i can t really explain it well   well  it s just  when i see a man even if he seems kind i suddenly get afraid  a cause is guessed and not confirmed   i wondered if something had happened in sakura s past to cause her intense fear of men   i know it would be good to simply say what it is i saw  but no matter what i do  i can t seem to imagine it  how can i speak that assertively","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p169-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.4: the night she asks him to come to her room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.169–175<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Evening, her dorm room 1106 on the eleventh floor — &quot;This was my first time setting foot there&quot; — reached by email rather than a call.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If I was absent from school tomorrow, what do you think would happen?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If it’s okay with you, could we meet right now? I’m in room 1106.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you could keep this a secret from everyone… That would really help me out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Come on in.&quot; — &quot;She greeted me wearing casual clothes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Umm… Ayanokouji-kun, do you remember what you said before? You said I wasn’t obligated to step forward, even though I was the witness. You also said it was meaningless to force me to testify.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I…just don’t have any self-confidence after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ve been terrible at it for so long… I’m not good at speaking in front of others. If I’m asked to testify in front of the teachers tomorrow, I don’t think I’ll have the confidence to answer properly. So…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ahhhhh. Jeez, why am I so completely useless?!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The outburst is new to him: &quot;It was the first time I’d seen her like that.&quot; and &quot;So she could be animated. I’d had no idea, considering her usually depressed look.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171–172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s because I’m not afraid of your eyes, Ayanokouji-kun…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, no. I don’t mean the eyes that you’ve seen me with. I mean the pupils, way back in the eyes… If you look someone deep in their eyes, you’ll understand. I’m sorry, I can’t really explain it well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, it’s just… When I see a man…even if he seems kind…I suddenly get afraid.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A cause is guessed and not confirmed: &quot;I wondered if something had happened in Sakura’s past to cause her intense fear of men.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I know it would be good to simply say what it is I saw. But no matter what I do, I can’t seem to imagine it… How can I speak that assertively?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p163-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.2: she testifies in the faculty room, and the teacher tests her<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p176-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.5: the club building, and advice she did not ask for<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p176-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5  5 5  the club building  and advice she did not ask for she takes him to the club activities building away from the school  the one  that hosted things like the archery club and the tea ceremony club  where arrows can be heard   i m not  but i ve wanted to come here at least once  i d stand out if i came by myself  so   why did you ask me to come out  anyway   horikita san  kushida san  ike kun  sudou kun  yamauchi kun   i don t know how to make friends at all  i m envious  you were the first person to call me a friend   yeah  i should apologize to kushida san sometime  she was the first one to call and invite me out  because i didn t have the courage  i actually wanted to hang out with her  i just couldn t answer her  no matter what i did  i m so pathetic   thank you  ayanokouji kun  whether the advice lands is left unresolved   hopefully  my words had found purchase somewhere in sakura s heart","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p176-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.5: the club building, and advice she did not ask for<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.176–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She takes him to the club-activities building away from the school, the one &quot;that hosted things like the archery club and the tea ceremony club&quot;, where arrows can be heard.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m not, but I’ve wanted to come here at least once. I’d stand out if I came by myself, so…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Why did you ask me to come out, anyway?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Horikita-san, Kushida-san, Ike-kun, Sudou-kun, Yamauchi-kun…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t know how to make friends at all. I’m envious. You were the first person to call me a friend.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah. I should apologize to Kushida-san sometime. She was the first one to call and invite me out, because I didn’t have the courage… I actually wanted to hang out with her. I just couldn’t answer her, no matter what I did. I’m so pathetic.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Thank you, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Whether the advice lands is left unresolved: &quot;Hopefully, my words had found purchase somewhere in Sakura’s heart.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p169-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.4: the night she asks him to come to her room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.6: the class finds out what she does with her face<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p179-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5  5 6  the class finds out what she does with her face ayanokoji s room  that night  kushida has called everyone but sudo  she is not present when the class identifies her  the blog is found by kushida  under the name shizuku  the proof the narrator offers is a dormitory door visible in one photograph  and his line is   you can barely see it  but the door to her dorm room is in this picture  the double life  stated plainly   she lived a double life as an idol and a quiet  inconspicuous student at our school  why she made the second life is not answered   why had she wanted to create another life  it was like a coin with two very different sides  the lensless glasses she dropped the night before are the disguise the class is now discussing  though not in her own words","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.6: the class finds out what she does with her face<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.179–181<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji&#x27;s room, that night; Kushida has called everyone but Sudō.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is not present when the class identifies her; the blog is found by Kushida, under the name Shizuku.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The proof the narrator offers is a dormitory door visible in one photograph, and his line is: &quot;You can barely see it, but the door to her dorm room is in this picture.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The double life, stated plainly: &quot;She lived a double life as an idol and a quiet, inconspicuous student at our school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Why she made the second life is not answered: &quot;Why had she wanted to create another life? It was like a coin with two very different sides.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The lensless glasses she dropped the night before are the disguise the class is now discussing, though not in her own words.<span class=\"pg\">p.180–181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p176-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.5: the club building, and advice she did not ask for<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p186-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.7: the comments that explain her fear<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p186-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5  5 7  the comments that explain her fear her blog ran about two years  starting when she began working as an idol  more than 5000 followers on twitter  she stopped replying after being accepted to the school  the record of one commenter escalates in public view   do you believe in fate  i do  i believe we will be together forever  then  look  god is real after all  the chapter s connection  kept as the narrator s inference  the electronics store clerk recognised her  and the repair form carried her real name and phone number  her fear at the repair counter is explained in hindsight by that inference  not by anything she says  nothing can be done before the hearing   in the end  the only option was to wait on an sos from the girl in question","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p186-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.7: the comments that explain her fear<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.186–188<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her blog ran about two years, starting when she began working as an idol; more than 5000 followers on Twitter; she stopped replying after being accepted to the school.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The record of one commenter escalates in public view: &quot;Do you believe in fate? I do. I believe we will be together forever.&quot; then &quot;Look, God is real after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s connection, kept as the narrator&#x27;s inference: the electronics-store clerk recognised her, and the repair form carried her real name and phone number.<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her fear at the repair counter is explained in hindsight by that inference, not by anything she says.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Nothing can be done before the hearing: &quot;In the end, the only option was to wait on an SOS from the girl in question.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.6: the class finds out what she does with her face<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p190-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the morning she comes anyway<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p190-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6 open  the morning she comes anyway the day of the hearing  she is in the classroom early  sitting alone  so as not to get roped into other students  conversations  her expression  even gloomier than usual   ah  yeah  i m fine   i thought that things would be tough if i were absent today  so  her attendance is a decision  not a habit  she came because  the entire class would be upset if she were absent   yeah  i ll be okay  she can tell ike and yamauchi know about the idol work  and answers the room without being asked  she  quietly mouthed the words   it s all right  the narrator credits the double life with the sensitivity   maybe working as an idol had made her sensitive to subtle changes in a room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p190-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 open: the morning she comes anyway<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.190<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The day of the hearing; she is in the classroom early, sitting alone &quot;so as not to get roped into other students’ conversations,&quot; her expression &quot;even gloomier than usual.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ah, yeah. I’m fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I thought that things would be tough if I were absent today, so…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah. I’ll be okay.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her attendance is a decision, not a habit: she came because &quot;the entire class would be upset if she were absent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She can tell Ike and Yamauchi know about the idol work, and answers the room without being asked: she &quot;quietly mouthed the words, &#x27;It’s all right.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narrator credits the double life with the sensitivity: &quot;Maybe working as an idol had made her sensitive to subtle changes in a room.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p186-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.7: the comments that explain her fear<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: the testimony that nearly does not start<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p191-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6  6 1  the testimony that nearly does not start class d s classroom at 3 50 pm  ten minutes before the hearing  she is  still sitting down  her body rigid  and stands with her lips trembling   yeah  i m okay  thank you   sakura was far tenser than i d expected    enough that the narrator fears she  might not be able to speak satisfactorily  the student council room on the fourth floor  she enters only when called   looking worried and restless  and  down at her feet  as if scared of danger   y yes  okay  well  i  the silence is measured on the page   ten seconds  twenty seconds  she looks further down and her face goes pale  horikita s prompt does not reach her  chabashira orders her to leave  she  closed her eyes tightly  as if she couldn t bear it anymore  as if she regretted her own weakness   i definitely saw what happened  the narrator does not recognise the voice at first  and what identifies her is volume   what most struck me was the volume of her voice   the students in class c threw the first punch  there s no mistake about that  the delivery carries force beyond her manner   she spoke so desperately that you wanted to believe she was telling the truth","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: the testimony that nearly does not start<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.191–200<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D’s classroom at 3:50 PM, ten minutes before the hearing; she is &quot;still sitting down, her body rigid&quot; and stands with her lips trembling. The student council room on the fourth floor; she enters only when called, &quot;looking worried and restless&quot; and &quot;down at her feet, as if scared of danger.&quot; Chabashira orders her to leave; she &quot;closed her eyes tightly, as if she couldn’t bear it anymore, as if she regretted her own weakness.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah… I’m okay. Thank you…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Y-yes, okay… Well… I…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I definitely saw what happened!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> &quot;Sakura was far tenser than I’d expected&quot; — enough that the narrator fears she &quot;might not be able to speak satisfactorily.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The silence is measured on the page: &quot;Ten seconds. Twenty seconds.&quot; She looks further down and her face goes pale; Horikita’s prompt does not reach her.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator does not recognise the voice at first, and what identifies her is volume: &quot;What most struck me was the volume of her voice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The students in Class C threw the first punch. There’s no mistake about that!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The delivery carries force beyond her manner: &quot;She spoke so desperately that you wanted to believe she was telling the truth.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p190-1\">← Before: Ch.6 open: the morning she comes anyway<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p202-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: the photographs<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p202-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6  6 1  the photographs  that s  well  that s  i didn t want to get involved   because i m not very good at talking with other people   that s  i m just telling the truth   n no  that s not it   if you want proof  i ll give it to you  she slams her hand on the desk and throws down what look like  a few small  rectangular pieces of paper    photographs  not paper   this is proof that i was in the special building that day   i m i was looking for places where no one was around so i could take pictures of myself  the pictures also show the date and time  which proves that i was there when i said   a digital camera  the photographs show her in the other life   this sakura wore a lovely expression that looked both similar and dissimilar to the sakura with us now  it was the idol  shizuku  the line presenting the decisive photo is untagged in the translation    i think that you ll believe i was there after seeing this    so it is recorded here without a speaker  the last photo shows the fight itself   the setting sun bathed the hallway in dusky light  and the image appears to be  what had happened immediately after sudou hit ishizaki","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p202-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: the photographs<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.202–205<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That’s… Well, that’s… I didn’t want to get involved…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Because I’m not very good at talking with other people…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That’s… I’m just…telling the truth…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;N-no, that’s not it…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you want proof… I’ll give it to you!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She slams her hand on the desk and throws down what look like &quot;a few small, rectangular pieces of paper&quot; — photographs, not paper.<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is proof that I was in the special building that day!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m…I was looking for places where no one was around so I could take pictures of myself. The pictures also show the date and time, which proves that I was there when I said.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A digital…camera.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The photographs show her in the other life: &quot;this Sakura wore a lovely expression that looked both similar and dissimilar to the Sakura with us now. It was the idol, Shizuku.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line presenting the decisive photo is untagged in the translation — &quot;I think that you’ll believe I was there after seeing…this.&quot; — so it is recorded here without a speaker.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The last photo shows the fight itself: &quot;The setting sun bathed the hallway in dusky light,&quot; and the image appears to be &quot;what had happened immediately after Sudou hit Ishizaki.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: the testimony that nearly does not start<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p209-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: after the hearing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p209-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6  6 1  after the hearing  i tried my absolute hardest to speak up during the discussion  but do we even have a chance  horikita   you understand that we won t solve this problem just by being stubborn  won t that just hurt more people in the process   i m sorry  ayanokouji kun  if i d only stepped forward in the very beginning  everything would have been fine  but  everything turned out this way because i didn t have the courage   but   i i i just told the truth   but it s all my fault  hic   but  i   but  i  wasn t i completely useless  the narrator s read of the crying   sakura seemed to be the type who bottled up her feelings  and the hearing  might have been an important step forward for her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p209-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: after the hearing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.209–212<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I tried my absolute hardest to speak up during the discussion, but do we even have a chance? Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You understand that we won’t solve this problem just by being stubborn. Won’t that just hurt more people in the process?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m sorry, Ayanokouji-kun… If I’d only stepped forward in the very beginning, everything would have been fine, but… Everything turned out this way because I didn’t have the courage.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I-I…I just…told the truth…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But…it’s all my fault… Hic.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But… I…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But… I… Wasn’t I completely useless?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narrator’s read of the crying: &quot;Sakura seemed to be the type who bottled up her feelings,&quot; and the hearing &quot;might have been an important step forward for her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p202-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: the photographs<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p213-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.2: walking out<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p213-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6  6 2  walking out  i let you see something so embarrassing   it s been such a long time since i cried in front of someone  i feel a little relieved  actually   i had no idea that you were like that  ayanokouji kun  that s completely unlike the image i have of you   i was really happy when you said that you believed me   yeah  but you came out and told me directly  ayanokouji kun  you said it   you gave me courage  i was happy   u um  well  i don t think i should be saying this now  but   actually  i  right now   oh  no  it s nothing  i just wanted to say that i would try my best  i ll be brave  the sentence she begins at the entranceway is cut off by ichinose s arrival and never resumed  she opens her shoe locker  gives the smaller answer  and hurries out when the narrator calls after her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.2: walking out<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.213–214<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I let you see something so embarrassing…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It’s been such a long time since I cried in front of someone. I feel a little relieved, actually.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I had no idea that you were like that, Ayanokouji-kun. That’s completely unlike the image I have of you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I was really happy…when you said that you believed me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah… But you came out and told me directly, Ayanokouji-kun. You said it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You gave me courage. I was happy,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;U-um, well… I don’t think I should be saying this now, but…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Actually… I… Right now…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, no, it’s nothing. I just…wanted to say that I would try my best. I’ll be brave.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The sentence she begins at the entranceway is cut off by Ichinose’s arrival and never resumed; she opens her shoe locker, gives the smaller answer, and hurries out when the narrator calls after her.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p209-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: after the hearing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p222-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1–7.2: the morning greeting and the last talk before the trial<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p222-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 7  7 1 7 2  the morning greeting and the last talk before the trial she is already at her desk when ayanokoji arrives   earlier than usual   sitting up straight   as if ready for something   um  good morning  ayanokouji kun  horikita san  the answer she gets back   g good morning  is printed with no speaker  the narrator only records that his own response stuck in his throat   ayanokouji kun  we re having the trial today   i see   it s because everyone s doing their best  i thought i d do my best  too  the page reads the line  felt like that she was saying that to herself  rather than to me   well  if there s something i need to move forward  i ll do it  her farewell smile and words  seemed so unlike her  and leave him with an unpleasant feeling   see you later  ayanokouji kun   i have plans today  maybe tomorrow","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p222-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.1–7.2: the morning greeting and the last talk before the trial<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.222–225<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She is already at her desk when Ayanokōji arrives — earlier than usual — sitting up straight, &quot;as if ready for something.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Um… Good morning, Ayanokouji-kun. Horikita-san.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ayanokouji-kun… We’re having the trial today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I see…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The answer she gets back, &quot;G-good morning…&quot;, is printed with no speaker; the narrator only records that his own response stuck in his throat.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s because everyone’s doing their best. I thought I’d do my best, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The page reads the line &quot;felt like that she was saying that to herself, rather than to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, if there’s something I need to move forward… I’ll do it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her farewell smile and words &quot;seemed so unlike her&quot; and leave him with an unpleasant feeling.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;See you later, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have plans today. Maybe tomorrow?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p213-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.2: walking out<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p236-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.4: the shuttered door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p236-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 7  7 4  the shuttered door at the electronics store entrance her fan   the store clerk who has been sending hundreds of letters to her room   catches her alone   please don t contact me anymore   stop  please  stop it   how do you know my room number  why do you keep sending these   please stop it  it s bothering me  she throws the bundle of letters to the floor  rejecting him   d don t come any closer  he latches onto her arm and shoves her against the store s shuttered door   no  let me go  she is  completely dumbfounded  by the delinquent tone ayanokoji puts on for the act  when the clerk runs she is exhausted enough to topple  and ayanokoji catches her arms and holds her up   ayanokouji  kun  why are you here   i guess i m no good after all  i couldn t do anything by myself in the end","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.4: the shuttered door<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.236–238<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the electronics-store entrance her fan — the store clerk who has been sending hundreds of letters to her room — catches her alone.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Please don’t contact me anymore!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Stop… Please, stop it!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;How do you know my room number? Why do you keep sending these?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Please stop it. It’s bothering me!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She throws the bundle of letters to the floor, rejecting him.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;D-don’t come any closer!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He latches onto her arm and shoves her against the store’s shuttered door.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, let me go!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is &quot;completely dumbfounded&quot; by the delinquent tone Ayanokōji puts on for the act.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When the clerk runs she is exhausted enough to topple, and Ayanokōji catches her arms and holds her up.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji… kun. Why are you here?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I guess I’m no good after all… I couldn’t do anything by myself in the end.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p222-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1–7.2: the morning greeting and the last talk before the trial<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p239-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.4: permission, and a footing with Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p239-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 7  7 4  permission  and a footing with class b she meets ayanokoji s eyes and gives him a slight nod   permission to tell ichinose the idol name   when did you realize  ayanokouji kun   but i never appeared on tv or anything   i think i m actually glad about this  though  it s been hard to lie   she laughed while seemingly on the verge of tears   ayanokouji kun  don t look at me with such strange eyes   never mind  it s nothing   do you think everyone would notice if i came to class without my glasses  and changed my hairstyle   okay  i understand  a little hesitant  she shakes ichinose s outstretched hand  the new footing is stated to her  if she suffers or feels lost she can talk to ayanokoji  and she should consult horikita and kushida too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p239-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.4: permission, and a footing with Class B<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.239–240<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;When did you realize, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;But I never appeared on TV or anything…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I think I’m actually glad about this, though… It’s been hard to lie.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She meets Ayanokōji’s eyes and gives him a slight nod — permission to tell Ichinose the idol name.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> &quot;She laughed while seemingly on the verge of tears.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun… Don’t look at me with such strange eyes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Never mind, it’s nothing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you think everyone would notice if I came to class without my glasses, and changed my hairstyle?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Okay. I understand,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> A little hesitant, she shakes Ichinose’s outstretched hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The new footing is stated to her: if she suffers or feels lost she can talk to Ayanokōji, and she should consult Horikita and Kushida too.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p236-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.4: the shuttered door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p48-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 2  the forest team  the blush  and the second volunteer shift walking from beach to forest  she is at the back  watching ayanokoji s back   and looks away when he turns  leftover paired with him and kouenji  trips on roots and he pulls her up  brushing dirt from her hands    s sorry     you don t need to apologize  flusters and hurries forward when he asks why she raised her hand   th that s not what i mean  it s just that since there isn t anyone i can talk to  that s why  lends her handkerchief for the trail marker without hesitation  goes  almost comatose  when he holds her hand through the class a hide    i thought i was going to die  my heart stopped    and adjusts her glasses as she recovers  surprisingly harsh on him in the moment   kouenji kun has been acting pretty funny from the start  so it s okay  scared off by a single sharp look    were you looking at me just now    and runs to put distance between them  second volunteer shift  the branch run  after sudou and yamauchi refuse   if i stay here  well it ll be a little uncomfortable  asks whether he should have taken ike s fire credit himself  his answer moves her    like she was moved by my words  eats alone at the edge of the groups  the boys  attention lands on her body while the chapter keeps her out of the conversation entirely  yamauchi s map of the class  she and horikita are the two girls  who are by themselves","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p48-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the forest team, the blush, and the second volunteer shift<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.48, p.52–63, p.74–97<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking from beach to forest; she is at the back, watching Ayanokōji&#x27;s back — and looks away when he turns.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Leftover-paired with him and Kouenji; trips on roots and he pulls her up, brushing dirt from her hands — &quot;S-sorry.&quot; / &quot;You don’t need to apologize.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Flusters and hurries forward when he asks why she raised her hand: &quot;Th-that’s not what I mean! It’s just that since there isn’t anyone I can talk to, that’s why…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Lends her handkerchief for the trail marker without hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Goes &quot;almost comatose&quot; when he holds her hand through the Class A hide — &quot;I thought I was going to die. My heart stopped…&quot; — and adjusts her glasses as she recovers.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Surprisingly harsh on him in the moment: &quot;Kouenji-kun has been acting pretty funny from the start, so it’s okay.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Scared off by a single sharp look — &quot;Were you looking at me just now?&quot; — and runs to put distance between them.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Second volunteer shift, the branch run, after Sudou and Yamauchi refuse; &quot;if I stay here, well…it’ll be…a little uncomfortable.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asks whether he should have taken Ike&#x27;s fire credit himself; his answer moves her — &quot;like she was moved by my words.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Eats alone at the edge of the groups; the boys&#x27; attention lands on her body while the chapter keeps her out of the conversation entirely.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Yamauchi&#x27;s map of the class: she and Horikita are the two girls &quot;who are by themselves.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p131-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: chasing him into the forest<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p131-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4  4 1  chasing him into the forest chases him out of base camp breathless on the third day and insists on coming along  rumors or not   ahh  ahh  ahh  wh where are you planning to go now  ayanokouji kun   i it s probably not okay for me to come along  is it  i d only slow you down  probably  but   that doesn t bother me at all  besides  i   th this is fun  though  offers more resistance to being left behind than he expects  after their eyes meet she crouches and hides her face   really  it s okay   no  not at all  we don t really talk or anything   i m just worthless  really  i can t do sports  or study  i m not really growing as a person in any area   huh  me  progress  ah ha ha  that s not true  though  absolute self devaluation   worthless  no growth in any area   delivered while twirling her hair with an index finger  with a laugh to wave off the encouragement  stops walking at his assurance  eyes trembling  to work out whether he means it   thank you for everything  everything worked out thanks to you  ayanokouji kun   no  everything s been fine  actually  i ve been taking a little break from the bulletin board  too  the stalker from the electronics store has resigned  and she has stepped back from the bulletin board as a precaution   well  that s that s because i did the photography myself   i didn t do well  and i also took way more time than the others  a cameraman would take pictures of the girls to make sure there were as few people involved as possible  besides back then  i was able to bear it because i made myself empty  it was like i erased myself  eliminated my feelings  but i eventually reached my limit  so i had to take a break  on the idol years  she made herself empty to get through the shoots and only broke when she reached her limit   spoken in one run  stopping at the end for a deep breath  the trip answer and the lines between the narration beats are untagged  they continue her own tagged speech  so they are recorded as hers   nature sure is amazing  isn t it  i like to spend a lot of my free time out in nature  even if it s just walking around   when we left for the trip  i felt depressed at first  i didn t have any friends  and i don t really like traveling  i thought it would be fine if i could just stay in my room  if i did that  my life would have been the same as always  but then  all this happened  we were told this was some kind of test   but now i m kind of glad that we came here  that s because i never really had the chance to talk with you like this before  ayanokouji kun  the two of them deep in the forest  embraced by nature and a feeling of serenity   i wish we could stay like this forever   oh  it s too bad  if i had my digital camera  i probably could have taken the best photos  but   no  if you re in the picture  ayanokouji kun  it will be the best photo  ah  no  i mean  that is  i ve never taken a picture with a friend before  frames herself and him with thumb and forefingers several times  then makes an embarrassed face at having done it  the camera habit runs deep enough to frame a shot that cannot be taken   and the new thing she names is a picture with a friend","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.1: chasing him into the forest<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.131–135<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chases him out of base camp breathless on the third day and insists on coming along, rumors or not.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ahh, ahh, ahh… Wh-where are you planning to go now, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I-It’s probably not okay for me…to come along, is it? I’d only slow you down, probably, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That doesn’t bother me at all. Besides, I….”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>24 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Th-this is fun, though!”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Offers more resistance to being left behind than he expects; after their eyes meet she crouches and hides her face.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really? It’s okay?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, not at all… We don’t really talk or anything,”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m just worthless, really. I can’t do sports, or study. I’m not really growing as a person in any area.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? Me, progress? Ah ha ha… That’s not true, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Absolute self-devaluation — worthless, no growth in any area — delivered while twirling her hair with an index finger, with a laugh to wave off the encouragement.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Stops walking at his assurance, eyes trembling, to work out whether he means it.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you for everything… Everything worked out thanks to you, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, everything’s been fine. Actually, I’ve been taking a little break from the bulletin board, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The stalker from the electronics store has resigned, and she has stepped back from the bulletin board as a precaution.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s…that’s because I did the photography myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t do well, and I also took way more time than the others. A cameraman would take pictures of the girls to make sure there were as few people involved as possible. Besides…back then, I was able to bear it because I made myself empty. It was like I erased myself, eliminated my feelings. But I eventually reached my limit, so I had to take a break.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> On the idol years: she made herself empty to get through the shoots and only broke when she reached her limit — spoken in one run, stopping at the end for a deep breath.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The trip answer and the lines between the narration beats are untagged; they continue her own tagged speech, so they are recorded as hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.133–135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nature sure is amazing, isn’t it? I like to spend a lot of my free time out in nature, even if it’s just walking around,”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When we left for the trip, I felt depressed at first. I didn’t have any friends, and I don’t really like traveling. I thought it would be fine if I could just stay in my room. If I did that, my life would have been the same as always. But then, all this happened. We were told this was some kind of test…”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But now I’m kind of glad that we came here. That’s because I never really had the chance to talk with you like this before, Ayanokouji-kun…”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The two of them deep in the forest, embraced by nature and a feeling of serenity.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wish we could stay like this forever…”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh… It’s too bad. If I had my digital camera, I probably could have taken the best photos, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, if you’re in the picture, Ayanokouji-kun, it will be the best photo… Ah! No! I mean, that is, I’ve never taken a picture with a friend before!”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Frames herself and him with thumb and forefingers several times, then makes an embarrassed face at having done it.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The camera habit runs deep enough to frame a shot that cannot be taken — and the new thing she names is a picture with a friend.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p48-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the forest team, the blush, and the second volunteer shift<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p137-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p137-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4  4 2  the caterpillar and the corn panics when he seizes her shoulders mid break   a caterpillar is in her hair  a fact he never tells her   wh what  what is it   wh what is it   n not at all  i absolutely can t stand them  ants either   o okay  sure   ugh i feel like there was something gross on me   umm  what s different  searches the bushes away from him and shrieks at something in them   hey  look  i found something amazing  finds a different variety of leaves and yellow ears inside a thicket   the discovery the trip was for   huh  wh wh wh what are you doing  ayanokouji kun  it s way too soon for that  drops the corn and covers her eyes with both hands when he takes his shirt off","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.137–140<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Panics when he seizes her shoulders mid-break — a caterpillar is in her hair, a fact he never tells her.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wh-what?! What is it?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wh-what is it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“N-not at all. I absolutely can’t stand them. Ants either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “O-okay. Sure…”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ugh…I feel like there was something gross on me…”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Umm… What’s different?”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Searches the bushes away from him and shrieks at something in them.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, look! I found something amazing!”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Finds a different variety of leaves and yellow ears inside a thicket — the discovery the trip was for.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh?! Wh-wh-wh-what are you doing, Ayanokouji-kun?! It’s way too soon for that!”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Drops the corn and covers her eyes with both hands when he takes his shirt off.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p131-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: chasing him into the forest<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p140-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: Katsuragi at the cornfield<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p140-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"katsuragi-kouhei totsuka-yahiko ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4  4 3  katsuragi at the cornfield jumps when katsuragi and yahiko arrive at the thicket and hides behind his back  draws his apology for the surprise   he saw where she had run to  his shout makes her jump again and curl into a ball  katsuragi answers with a thump to his head  ike s camp greeting names her as one of the two who found the food  the jealousy scene runs over her  he shoves ayanokoji away from her side before the whole camp  leaves the thicket with him while she still looks worried  back at base camp for the report  the harvest team forms soon after and everyone is back by one o clock","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p140-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.3: Katsuragi at the cornfield<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.140–142<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Jumps when Katsuragi and Yahiko arrive at the thicket and hides behind his back.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Back at base camp for the report; the harvest team forms soon after and everyone is back by one o’clock.<span class=\"pg\">p.141–142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Draws his apology for the surprise — he saw where she had run to.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> His shout makes her jump again and curl into a ball; Katsuragi answers with a thump to his head.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Ike’s camp greeting names her as one of the two who found the food.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The jealousy scene runs over her: he shoves Ayanokōji away from her side before the whole camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Leaves the thicket with him while she still looks worried.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p137-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p171-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: speaking up<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p171-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei kushida-kikyou sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6  6 1  speaking up cowering behind everyone  she speaks up for ayanokoji when no other girl will   and becomes karuizawa s next target  speaks in his defense when the girls turn on him  the narration notes she dislikes being noticed more than anything   um  i don t think that a ayanokouji kun would do such a thing  fidgets bashfully with her back arched  cowering behind everyone   a bold act for her  karuizawa changes her target to her the instant she speaks  lashing out as if sinking her teeth into prey   well that s because he isn t that kind of person   y you re wrong  runs off into the forest under the teasing  kushida chases after her  chases after her into the woods  judging it dangerous to go alone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: speaking up<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.171–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Cowering behind everyone, she speaks up for Ayanokōji when no other girl will — and becomes Karuizawa’s next target.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Um… I don’t think that A-Ayanokouji-kun would do such a thing…”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well…that’s because…he isn’t that kind of person.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Y-you’re wrong!”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Speaks in his defense when the girls turn on him; the narration notes she dislikes being noticed more than anything.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Fidgets bashfully with her back arched, cowering behind everyone — a bold act for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Karuizawa changes her target to her the instant she speaks, lashing out as if sinking her teeth into prey.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Runs off into the forest under the teasing; Kushida chases after her.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Chases after her into the woods, judging it dangerous to go alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p140-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.3: Katsuragi at the cornfield<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p194-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.4: the forest search<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p194-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6  6 4  the forest search on the last forage with yamauchi watching her  she trails the pair that heads off with horikita   eh  o oh  it s okay  i m fine  leans forward to avoid yamauchi s gaze  he looks for excuses to talk to her while staring at her chest  trails behind horikita and ayanokoji with her shoulders slumped as the pairs form","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p194-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.4: the forest search<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.194–199<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the last forage with Yamauchi watching her, she trails the pair that heads off with Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Eh? O-oh, it’s okay. I’m fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Leans forward to avoid Yamauchi’s gaze.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> He looks for excuses to talk to her while staring at her chest.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Trails behind Horikita and Ayanokōji with her shoulders slumped as the pairs form.<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p171-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: speaking up<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p201-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.5: waiting for the shower<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p201-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6  6 5  waiting for the shower refuses the river behind ibuki s lead and keeps her place in the shower line   w well  i will  too  stays in the line rather than swim   she does not want the boys to see her in a swimsuit  takes her refusal from ibuki  the two wait in line together behind karuizawa s group","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p201-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.5: waiting for the shower<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.201–202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Refuses the river behind Ibuki’s lead and keeps her place in the shower line.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“W-well, I will, too…”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stays in the line rather than swim — she does not want the boys to see her in a swimsuit.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Takes her refusal from Ibuki; the two wait in line together behind Karuizawa’s group.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p194-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.4: the forest search<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p15-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 2  one of the three named in ayanokoji s recollection of the people he could talk to in the first semester  listed with horikita and kushida as the three he talked with   his school life hadn t been all that bad","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: one of the three<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.15<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Ayanokōji’s recollection of the people he could talk to in the first semester.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Listed with Horikita and Kushida as the three he talked with — his school life hadn’t been all that bad.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: the roommate appeal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou shinohara-satsuki ichihashi-ruri maezono ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 2  2 2  the roommate appeal emails ayanokoji to the second deck and stammers through her roommate worry  flees when kushida appears   wah  a ayanokouji kun   n no  no  i m just kind of strangely nervous is all  nervous to the point of jolt like surprise  her normally hunched posture straightens at once   ayanokouji kun  you re roommates with hirata kun  kouenji kun  and yukimura kun  right   oh  well  to tell you the truth  i i m a little worried about the people i m sharing a room with   i m not sure  i have mixed feelings  i do want to get along with them  but i also want to be alone  too  i m just hopeless  aren t i   oh  didn t i tell you  shinohara san  ichihashi san  and maezono san   i just thought any advice from you  ayanokouji kun  would be good   i i m sorry to just come to you for help like this out of the blue  you re so busy  ayanokouji kun   retreated as fast as her legs would carry her  at kushida s arrival  rejection and flight  kushida s brightness lands as threat  names her as roommate one  the narration adds shinohara won t go out of her way for her  roommate two   named only  no file yet  first appearance volume  roommate three   named only  no file yet  comes to him because  any advice from you would be good","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2: the roommate appeal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.25–28<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Emails Ayanokōji to the second deck and stammers through her roommate worry; flees when Kushida appears.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#ichihashi-ruri\">Ichihashi Ruri<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#maezono\">Maezono<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wah! A-Ayanokouji-kun?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“N-no, no. I’m just kind of strangely nervous is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayanokouji-kun, you’re roommates with Hirata-kun, Kouenji-kun, and Yukimura-kun. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Nervous to the point of jolt-like surprise; her normally hunched posture straightens at once.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh. Well, to tell you the truth, I…I’m a little worried about the people I’m sharing a room with.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not sure. I have mixed feelings. I do want to get along with them, but I also want to be alone, too. I’m just hopeless, aren’t I?”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh. Didn’t I tell you? Shinohara-san, Ichihashi-san, and Maezono-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I…just thought any advice from you, Ayanokouji-kun, would be good?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I-I’m sorry to just come to you for help like this out of the blue. You’re so busy, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> “retreated as fast as her legs would carry her” at Kushida’s arrival.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Rejection and flight; Kushida’s brightness lands as threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Names her as roommate one; the narration adds Shinohara won’t go out of her way for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichihashi Ruri<\/b> Roommate two — named only; no file yet (first appearance volume).<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Maezono<\/b> Roommate three — named only; no file yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Comes to him because “any advice from you…would be good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25–28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p15-1\">← Before: Ch.2: one of the three<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: the bow stress-talk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p97-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki sudou-ken ike-kanji matsushita-chiaki sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 3  3 2  the bow stress talk waits behind a pillar on the bow deck after moving from the crowded elevator route  mutters to herself  hands ayanokoji the cow roster  and finds the one person who will take her call   i was thinking about it  but h how do i do it  she murmured out loud   before he arrives   self talk over the wind   aaaieeeeeeeeeeee  sakura yelped  practically jumping out of her own skin  seemed like i d surprised her after all   wh wh when did you get here  how much did you hear  she asked frantically   were you listening  did you hear what i was saying  sakura shouted   um  well  you see  it s ah  i was s stressing out over the test  she shouted  hands him a list   the cow group names by class   looking incredibly depressed   i thought i might know someone from another class but amazingly enough  i don t know anyone  no one who would remotely consider me a   friend  said sakura   ah  it s okay  you don t need to apologize  it s just that i don t have any friends  sakura responded   huh  me  what is it   yamauchi kun  no  he hasn t  is something the matter  she asked   on yamauchi contact   is that okay  asked sakura   after he offers to be her contact   i ll definitely contact you  she said  eyes sparkle like a child s  a little different from her usual self   overjoyed  more vigor  maybe more assertive  the island test  changed her life in unexpected ways  and she has learned to stay positive  the loner pact  the contact offer  and the secret he keeps about yamauchi s email promise  names him as not having been in touch  does not know the email promise  on her cow roster as a class d boy she is stuck with  the other class d boy on the roster  the fourth class d name on her list","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.2: the bow stress-talk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.97–102<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits behind a pillar on the bow deck after moving from the crowded elevator route; mutters to herself, hands Ayanokōji the Cow roster, and finds the one person who will take her call.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#matsushita-chiaki\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I was thinking about it, but…h-how do I do it?” she murmured out loud. (before he arrives — self-talk over the wind)<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Aaaieeeeeeeeeeee!” Sakura yelped, practically jumping out of her own skin. Seemed like I’d surprised her after all. “Wh-wh-when did you get here? How much did you hear?” she asked frantically.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Were you listening?! Did you hear what I was saying?!” Sakura shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Um, well. You see, it’s…ah… I was s-stressing out over the test!” she shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands him a list — the Cow group names by class — looking incredibly depressed.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I thought I might know someone from another class but…amazingly enough, I don’t know anyone. No one who would remotely consider me a … friend,” said Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.100-101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, it’s okay. You don’t need to apologize. It’s just that…I don’t have any friends!” Sakura responded.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? Me? What is it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yamauchi-kun? No, he hasn’t. Is something the matter?” she asked. (on Yamauchi contact)<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that okay?” asked Sakura. (after he offers to be her contact)<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll definitely contact you!” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Eyes sparkle like a child’s; a little different from her usual self — overjoyed, more vigor, maybe more assertive; the island test “changed her life in unexpected ways” and she has learned to stay positive.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The loner pact, the contact offer, and the secret he keeps about Yamauchi’s email promise.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Names him as not having been in touch; does not know the email promise.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> On her Cow roster as a Class D boy she is stuck with.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The other Class D boy on the roster.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> The fourth Class D name on her list.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the roommate appeal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p103-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the email-address standoff<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p103-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 3  the email address standoff yamauchi corners ayanokoji over the promise he never made  yamauchi shouts that ayanokoji was talking with sakura just now and was after her all along  ayanokoji refuses to hand over sakura s contact information without her consent  then asks whether yamauchi means to make sakura tell him  yamauchi bursts at the chance of a new camera for sakura  ayanokoji tells him to earn it first so he deserves a former idol","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the email-address standoff<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.103–105<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yamauchi corners Ayanokōji over the promise he never made.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Yamauchi shouts that Ayanokōji was talking with Sakura just now and was after her all along.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji refuses to hand over Sakura’s contact information without her consent, then asks whether Yamauchi means to make Sakura tell him.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Yamauchi bursts at the chance of a new camera for Sakura; Ayanokōji tells him to earn it first so he deserves a former idol.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p97-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: the bow stress-talk<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.3: a pair of assets<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p116-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 3  a pair of assets named as one of the two people ayanokoji might still be able to use  he counts horikita and sakura as potential eyes and ears while planning his next move","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: a pair of assets<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.116<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as one of the two people Ayanokōji might still be able to use.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He counts Horikita and Sakura as potential eyes and ears while planning his next move.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p103-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the email-address standoff<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the meek comparison<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p179-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4  the meek comparison her name becomes the measure for the meek  bullied type  the narration contrasts personalities like sakura against karuizawa s confident  selfish type  another girl with them seems meek  rather like sakura   probably rika","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the meek comparison<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.179, p.189<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her name becomes the measure for the meek, bullied type.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narration contrasts personalities like Sakura against Karuizawa’s confident, selfish type.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Another girl with them seems meek, rather like Sakura — probably Rika.<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.3: a pair of assets<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p183-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.5: the Cow group ends<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p183-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke sudou-ken katsuragi-kouhei sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4  4 5  the cow group ends calls ayanokoji after the cow group early end email  denies the vip role  reports class a s silence  and waves goodbye   yeah  she replied   have i done something wrong  she asked  the cow group has ended   same notice the monkey group got  she reads unease into it  his monkey ending is the comparison ayanokoji uses for the cow email   two different betrayal motives  certainty vs impatience   no  you haven t  this just means that someone in the cow group reported to the school who they think the vip is   his line  in exchange   sakura  were you the vip  or was it someone else   his line   no  i m not the vip  but i m not sure about sudou kun or  um  the others  she answered  names him in the uncertain cow roster   no idea whether he or the others were the vip   okay  thank you  ayanokouji kun  i m happy you told me that   how are things with class a  i heard rumors that none of them are participating in the discussions   his line   yeah  it s just like what the others have been saying  none of them have talked at all  said sakura  the class a silence confirmed from her side   katsuragi s plan  rather thorough   if there s anything else  please let me know  you can talk to me anytime  i told sakura   thank you  ayanokouji kun  see you later  waves her hands adorably on the goodbye   the meek profile he filed against karuizawa s type","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p183-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.5: the Cow group ends<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.183–184<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Calls Ayanokōji after the Cow-group early-end email; denies the VIP role, reports Class A’s silence, and waves goodbye.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah…” she replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Have I done something wrong?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No, you haven’t. This just means that someone in the Cow group reported to the school who they think the VIP is.” (his line, in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The Cow group has ended — same notice the Monkey group got; she reads unease into it.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> His Monkey ending is the comparison Ayanokōji uses for the Cow email — two different betrayal motives (certainty vs impatience).<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sakura, were you the VIP? Or was it someone else?” (his line)<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I’m not the VIP. But I’m not sure about Sudou-kun or, um, the others,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Names him in the uncertain Cow roster — no idea whether he or the others were the VIP.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. Thank you, Ayanokouji-kun. I’m happy you told me that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How are things with Class A? I heard rumors that none of them are participating in the discussions.” (his line)<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, it’s just like what the others have been saying. None of them have talked at all,” said Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The Class A silence confirmed from her side — Katsuragi’s plan “rather thorough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If there’s anything else, please let me know. You can talk to me anytime,” I told Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you, Ayanokouji-kun. See you later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Waves her hands adorably on the goodbye — the meek profile he filed against Karuizawa’s type.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the meek comparison<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p28-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 2  a passing mention in the partner list named once as the one girl who would probably come   and the reason he does not ask her  the couples floor would make her uncomfortable   i felt like sakura would probably come with me  but if i brought her to a place positively teeming with couples  it d make her uncomfortable","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p28-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: a passing mention in the partner list<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.28<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as the one girl who would probably come — and the reason he does not ask her.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The couples floor would make her uncomfortable: “I felt like Sakura would probably come with me, but if I brought her to a place positively teeming with couples, it’d make her uncomfortable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p41-1\">→ After: Ch.2: a passing mention in the rescue call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p41-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 2  a passing mention in the rescue call named once as the quiet option that still would not work  gossip free but easily flustered   sakura wouldn t gossip  but the situation would probably fluster her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p41-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: a passing mention in the rescue call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.41<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as the quiet option that still would not work.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Gossip-free but easily flustered: “Sakura wouldn’t gossip, but the situation would probably fluster her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p28-1\">← Before: Ch.2: a passing mention in the partner list<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p49-1\">→ After: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p49-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"inogashira-kokoro sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 3  a passing mention ak compares inogashira to sakura   a somewhat quiet  plain girl from class d  rather like sakura  the comparison is the only footprint sakura has in this chapter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.49<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">AK compares Inogashira to Sakura: “a somewhat quiet, plain girl from Class D, rather like Sakura.”<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"index.html#inogashira-kokoro\">Inogashira Kokoro<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Inogashira Kokoro<\/b> The comparison is the only footprint Sakura has in this chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p41-1\">← Before: Ch.2: a passing mention in the rescue call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p83-1\">→ After: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p83-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 3  a passing mention named as the girl yamauchi is aiming for while he enjoys kushida s company on the walk  the narration notes kushida s charms reach him even with sakura on his mind","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p83-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.83<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the girl Yamauchi is aiming for while he enjoys Kushida&#x27;s company on the walk.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The narration notes Kushida&#x27;s charms reach him even with Sakura on his mind.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p49-1\">← Before: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p122-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the one who had water<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p122-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4  the one who had water ak s chat asking to borrow water goes unread  he assumes she is asleep  her late reply opens the way to real water  horikita asks that she never learn who was stuck  she replies that she was researching and didn t notice the message   you wanted water  right   i ll wait for you  texting with her goes smoothly where talking in person is difficult","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p122-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the one who had water<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.122, 130<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">AK&#x27;s chat asking to borrow water goes unread; he assumes she is asleep. She replies that she was researching and didn&#x27;t notice the message.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You wanted water, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll wait for you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her late reply opens the way to real water; Horikita asks that she never learn who was stuck.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Texting with her goes smoothly where talking in person is difficult.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p83-1\">← Before: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p137-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: the letter<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p137-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5  5 1  the letter kushida s invitation brings her behind the school building  finding only ak is a relief  she doesn t normally talk to kushida and feared she had done something to make her angry   i don t normally talk to kushida san  so i was worried i did something to make her angry   but why get kushida s help  ayanokouji kun   a l letter behind the school  a boy   ah  ahhh  th this is  oh my  oh my  ahhh  she stammers to a standstill once the words love letter come out   what about horikita san   eh  i it s not from you  ayanokouji kun   but i can t i can t do it  i can t   never   will you read it with me   that s not possible now   i i ll try reading it  she hangs her head and leaves to read the letter alone in her room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.1: the letter<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.137–143<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida&#x27;s invitation brings her behind the school building; finding only AK is a relief.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t normally talk to Kushida-san, so I was worried I did something to make her angry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“But why get Kushida’s help, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“A l-letter…behind the school… A boy…”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She doesn&#x27;t normally talk to Kushida and feared she had done something to make her angry.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, ahhh. Th-this is… Oh my. Oh my. Ahhh!”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She stammers to a standstill once the words love letter come out.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What about…Horikita-san?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Eh? I-It’s not from you, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I can’t…I can’t do it! I can’t…”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Never!”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Will you read it with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not possible now,”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I-I’ll try reading it!”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She hangs her head and leaves to read the letter alone in her room.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p122-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the one who had water<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p144-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the night call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p144-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5  5 2  the night call her midnight texts become a phone call  tomorrow s answer keeps her awake   are you awake   did i wake you   i have to meet with yamauchi kun at five tomorrow  but can i meet you before that   is it okay if i call you   i i don t know anything about yamauchi kun   i just realized that liking someone  or hating someone  actually comes with a ton of responsibility   yamauchi kun hasn t done anything wrong  but this  i think i just don t want this   that s what i m wondering   are you perhaps dating anyone at the present time   r really   i was happy because you re like me  that s all   oh  you   has anyone ever confessed their feelings to you   okay  i see  she sounds happy again  they chat until she grows drowsy and the call ends","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2: the night call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.144–146<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her midnight texts become a phone call; tomorrow&#x27;s answer keeps her awake.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you awake?”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Did I wake you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I have to meet with Yamauchi-kun at five tomorrow, but…can I meet you before that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it okay if I call you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I-I don’t know anything about Yamauchi-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just realized that liking someone, or hating someone, actually comes with a ton of responsibility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yamauchi-kun hasn’t done anything wrong, but this… I think I just don’t want this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s what I’m wondering.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “are you perhaps dating anyone at the…present time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “R-really?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was happy because you’re like me, that’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “has anyone ever confessed their feelings to you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, I see!”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She sounds happy again; they chat until she grows drowsy and the call ends.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p137-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.1: the letter<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p147-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3: the rejection<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p147-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5  5 3  the rejection she waits ten minutes early with a pained  shifting look  rain soaks them before the answer   thank you for coming here  ayanokouji kun   it s raining   i i m fine   i m surprisingly tough  you know  she dries his hair and face with the island handkerchief  the handkerchief is the one she lent him on the uninhabited island   i i wonder what i should do   i m going to turn him down   i don t think i m qualified to reject someone   please don t leave me alone   wh why do you like me   i i m sorry   i can t  um  return your feelings   g goodbye","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p147-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.3: the rejection<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.147–152<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She waits ten minutes early with a pained, shifting look; rain soaks them before the answer.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Thank you for coming here, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s raining,”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I-I’m fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m surprisingly tough, you know,”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She dries his hair and face with the island handkerchief.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The handkerchief is the one she lent him on the uninhabited island.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I…I wonder what I should do…”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to turn him down.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think I’m qualified to reject someone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please don’t leave me alone,”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wh-why do you like…me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I…I’m sorry!”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t, um, return your feelings”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “G-goodbye!”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4_5-p144-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.2: the night call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
